# Environment variables for ihaveallergy.com
#
# Classification of every variable this app reads. Vite inlines anything
# prefixed VITE_ into the client bundle at build time, so a VITE_ variable is
# published to every visitor by definition. Never put a secret behind that
# prefix.
#
# ── PUBLIC / SAFE FOR CLIENT ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shipped in the JavaScript bundle. Public by design. The anon key carries
# role "anon" and grants only what row-level security allows.

VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-ref"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="your-anon-key"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"

# ── SERVER ONLY / SECRET ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are NOT in this file and must never be. They are configured as
# Supabase Edge Function secrets and are readable only inside a function via
# Deno.env.get(). Listed here so the full set is documented in one place:
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   SECRET — bypasses RLS entirely, full DB access
#   RESEND_API_KEY              SECRET — transactional email
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID          SECRET — WhatsApp / SMS
#   TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN           SECRET
#   TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID   SECRET
#   TWILIO_WHATSAPP_FROM        SERVER ONLY
#   LOVABLE_API_KEY             SECRET — AI gateway
#   REMINDER_INTERNAL_TOKEN     SECRET — internal cron authentication
#   SITE_URL                    SERVER ONLY
#
# Added by the Stage 1 search/analytics integration (see the setup notes):
#   GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON SECRET — service account for GSC + GA4 read
#   GSC_SITE_URL                SERVER ONLY — the verified Search Console property
#   GA4_PROPERTY_ID             SERVER ONLY — numeric GA4 property id
